   788	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G04]
   789	- **Qualifying ("verified") attestation.** A Bitcoin attestation at height h qualifies if and only if (a) the
   790	  bundled header at h exists and its merkle root equals the attestation message; (b) headers h … h+5 are all
   791	  bundled; (c) each equals its pin, `hex(reverse(SHA256d(header))) = pin[height]`; (d) for i = h+1 … h+5,
   792	  `header_i.prev = SHA256d(header_{i−1})`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` what 'verified' means
   793	  for an attestation", 2026-10-13.)*
   794	- **Selection.** Attestation selection is existential over qualifying branches. A syntactically valid Bitcoin
   795	  attestation without a complete h..h+5 segment is nonqualifying, not a required failed check. It supplies no time or
   796	  trust fact. All supplied headers, including unused ones, are independently checked against pins (section 7.2).
   797	  The selected anchor, rather than every unverified attestation, is the referent of "anchors beyond the newest pin"
   798	  (A9 C6 as revised 2026-10-14). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05]
   799	- **Proof outcomes.** A pinned bundled header at h whose merkle root ≠ the attestation message: `INVALID /
   800	  OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH` (a contradicted branch fails the proof). No qualifying attestation: `UNVERIFIABLE /
   801	  HEADERS_MISSING` if any Bitcoin attestation is present, `UNVERIFIABLE / ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY` if only pending ones;
   802	  the snapshot uses `SNAPSHOT_NOT_ANCHORED` and git `GIT_NOT_ANCHORED`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05]
   803	- **Time arithmetic.** Times are integer seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z without leap seconds; nTime is the
   804	  header's uint32; RFC 3339 fields convert by days-from-civil (proleptic Gregorian); comparisons are inclusive.
   805	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G03]
