   818	### 7.2 Header pins
   819	
   820	- Every bundle header must be in the pinned set. Otherwise the verdict is `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`.
   821	  There is no retarget logic, because the pins cover every accepted header. [A9:150; DD:99]
   822	- **Conflict.** A supplied header at a pinned height with a different hash gives `INVALID / HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`:
   823	  it is contradictory evidence. A9.1's "a bundle header outside the pins" is read as a header **at a height the pins
   824	  do not cover**. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G23] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` the verdict for a header that … conflicts with a
   825	  pin", 2026-10-13.)*
   826	- **Coverage.** Required: headers h* … h*+5 of the selected attestation of each of the three proofs (receipt,
   827	  snapshot, git), all in the shared `headers` pool. Every supplied header, used or not, is checked against the pins.
   828	  A `headers` entry that fails row 2.4 is not a supplied header: it contributes `CONTAINER_SCHEMA` only, and rows
   829	  10.x, 11.x, 13.4 and 14.6 use the remaining entries [OWNER 2026-10-14, diff-1 F-3].
   830	  For each pair of supplied headers at consecutive heights, a prev-hash mismatch gives `INVALID /
   831	  HEADER_CHAIN_BROKEN`; a missing intermediate height is not a broken link. No PoW, nBits or retarget check: a hash
   832	  equal to a pin implies all of it. At an unselected height, a pinned header with missing successors is ignored,
   833	  while an unpinned header blocks the bundle (`HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G07, G05] *(Was: "`OPEN
   834	  (step 8):` which heights the pins must cover for a given proof", 2026-10-13.)*
